# Two copied Structures with different bodies: A needs the free name x, B the
# free name y, both int, each at the same input position of its own contract.
# Each call of a copy forms the inputs of the body that copy really holds --
# the caller's current x for ra, its current y for rb, a changed working value
# included -- and runs the copy, never the prototype. A copy's node is its own
# copy of the unit (merge parent): its seen write raises that copy's seen (ra's
# 11 then 16, rb's 29; the post paths read them), never the unit's, which stays
# 0. Entry 7.
int: seen 0
A:
    int: last 0
    last: x
    node\seen: node\seen + x
B:
    int: last 0
    last: y
    node\seen: node\seen + y
int: x 11
int: y 29
ra: merge: A
rb: merge: B
@: int ps @seen
int: result 7
ra
if: ra\last != 11 || A\last != 0 || \ps != 0
    result: 81
rb
if: rb\last != 29 || B\last != 0 || \ps != 0
    result: 82
x: 5
ra
if: ra\last != 5 || rb\last != 29 || \ps != 0
    result: 83
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: result; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
